"""Detect forms of 'be', using only the current and preceding token.

' is' is strongly positive after ordinary words, word pieces, numbers, and
punctuation. Several pronoun-shaped tokens attenuate it; 'what is' is negative.
Smaller constant responses cover other forms of 'be' and some equivalents in European
languages. These surface rules do not parse or infer a grammatical subject.
